%% Sequence diagram: a user reports a problem and the admin bans the offender
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Non-admin user
  actor A as Admin
  participant RV as ReportView
  participant AW as AdminWelcomeScreen
  participant SV as server.py
  participant DC as database_core
  participant DB as users.db
  U->>RV: fill category, offender, summary, details
  RV->>SV: POST /api/reports
  SV->>DC: create_report()
  DC->>DB: check reporter (not banned, not admin, max 5 open)
  DC->>DB: INSERT reports (Open)
  A->>AW: open Reports
  AW->>SV: GET /api/admin/reports?admin_email=
  SV->>DC: get_reports(admin) with is_admin check
  DC-->>AW: open reports first
  A->>AW: Ban offender
  AW->>SV: POST /api/admin/users/ban
  SV->>DC: set_user_banned(admin, email)
  DC->>DB: UPDATE users SET banned = 1 (not self, not an admin)
  AW->>SV: POST /api/admin/reports/{id}/resolve
  SV->>DC: resolve_report()
  Note over U,DB: Next login of the banned user returns 403 and _blocked() refuses its writes
